From 2d4a8050b89e1065fd5d98bd6e0b3a5e87b3093b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 11:30:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: measure the q6_K q8_1 MMVQ route at verify widths,
 ship it as a switch, keep the default

DECIDER (r71-evidence/13-paired.txt, one binary, 6 interleaved and counterbalanced rounds, paired per round, arms by env only). default/mmvq median, wins/6: 248320x5120 n=7 1.400 6/6, n=8 1.131 6/6, but n=4 0.909 0/6 and n=5 0.735 0/6. 17408x5120 n=7 1.122 6/6, n=8 1.085 6/6, n=1 1.043 6/6, n=2..5 all lose. 5120x17408 n=7 1.163 6/6, n=8 1.050 6/6, n=2 1.054 5/6, n=3 1.046 5/6, n=5 0.914 0/6, n=6 0.958 1/6. 24 plain cells EXECUTED: 11 admit, 12 loss, 1 short of the bar. m=5120 k=6144 executed 0 cells (test-backend-ops carries no such MUL_MAT case) and is reported absent, not as a tie.

WHY THE DEFAULT DOES NOT MOVE. The qualifying widths are a non-contiguous island and the row geometry does not explain them. Geometry alone predicts a clean sign flip at n=5 (f32 rm_kq=2 rows at every width :7555 against MMVQ rm_int_n(rm_kq_int=1,i) 1 row at NUM_COLS<=4 and 4 at >=5 :7666, the exact pair that made the Q5_K n>=5 admit a rule), and n=5 is instead the WORST cell on all three shapes. The raw us/run show two shaders with two different width cliffs: f32 jumps at n=6,7 (13882 -> 20967 -> 20046 us on 248320x5120) and MMVQ jumps at n=5,6 (15245 -> 20971 -> 21121). The n=7,8 win is the gap between two defects, not evidence that MMVQ is the right route, so a rule fitted to it is overfitting. Both cliffs are the brief for a q6_K shader lane. This is the third outcome pre-registered at 08907df1b section 3c, and the standing GGML_ARIFI_ROCMFP4_MMVQ is already held to: measured, kept, reachable, default OFF until an independent checker clears it.

MUL_MAT_ID is EXCLUDED on evidence. 26 executed _id cells over the same 6 rounds gave 1 admit, 9 losses and ~1.00 medians on the rest (16-paired-id.txt) -- a wash. Admitting it would move the arithmetic for 88 percent of Ornith-1.5's q6_K bytes, 21.3 percent of that whole file, for nothing. That needed a new is_id flag because MUL_MAT (:12656) and MUL_MAT_ID (:13944) share this predicate; every other rule ignores the flag, so no existing route moves. The trace dedup key gains op= for the same reason.

ROOT FIX carried here, not a patch. The R48c 0/1 parser read "anything that is not 0 means 1". That was safe while 0 and 1 were the only values and is a trap the moment the variable gains names: under it BOTH new names parsed as 1 and force-routed q6_K at every width, so GGML_ARIFI_Q6K_MMVQ=legacy would silently have been the opposite of legacy. Caught by the shipped-switch trace showing both arms identical. Only the exact strings 0 and 1 are the diagnostic now.

Shipped-switch trace, three arms, one binary (12-trace-ship-*.txt): legacy routes 0 MUL_MAT and 0 MUL_MAT_ID cells to MMVQ; route routes exactly n=7,8 at k=5120 and n=2,3,7,8 at k=17408 and 0 MUL_MAT_ID; the =1 diagnostic still reaches all 16 MUL_MAT widths and 15 MUL_MAT_ID cells.

DEFAULT IS UNCHANGED, so the shipped serve path is byte-identical to before this commit and the served effect of the default is zero by construction. Served t/s of the route arm: UNMEASURED.

Origin: lane-256 R71, q6_K mat-vec at verify widths n=2..8 on AMD
Measured-effect: op-level on gfx1103, 6 interleaved counterbalanced rounds, paired; with GGML_ARIFI_Q6K_MMVQ=route n=7 is 1.400x on 248320x5120, 1.163x on 5120x17408, 1.122x on 17408x5120 and n=8 is 1.131x/1.050x/1.085x, all 6/6 rounds; the DEFAULT is unchanged so the shipped serve path is byte-identical and its served effect is zero by construction.
Lane: lane-256
Cherry-picked-from: 088cf4e0f (ArifiLabs lane-256 R71, onto arifi/main 94461e770)
Conflict-resolved: S4 split (f172be756): auto_split - our hunks re-homed into ggml-vulkan-types.h; wrap/same-point regions merged in place (fixS4_659.py)
